<title>USA: King County, Wash., bans tobacco ads near schools.</title>
<headline>King County, Wash., bans tobacco ads near schools.</headline>
<dateline>SEATTLE 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The King County Board of Health Friday voted unanimously to ban tobacco advertising within 2,000 feet of schools and playgrounds.</p>
<p>The board's action, aimed at reversing a recent increase in smoking by minors, takes effect Aug. 15.</p>
<p>The board originally had proposed banning tobacco billboards within 1,000 feet of schools and playgrounds but decided to double the distance to provide a &quot;stronger level of protection,&quot; said Chairman Greg Nickels.</p>
